    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199-a1">

                <pb facs="0375" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg313"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 18.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Smith to Mr.
                            Welsh</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">At
                                Portland</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 26,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: I have received, both officially
                    and privately, reports of the warm and hearty hospitality with which our
                    squadron, under the command of Admiral Inglefield, <pb facs="0376" n="314"
                        xml:id="pg314"/> has been received at Newport, R. I., and I hope I shall not
                    occasion you trouble if I beg on behalf of the admiralty that you will cause
                    their very sincere thanks to be conveyed to the governor of Rhode Island and to
                    the mayor of Newport for the cordial reception which was accorded to the
                    officers and sailors of the fleet.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. H. SMITH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
